# Settings live preview (required)

Owner settings that change the public or member site must use the **live iframe preview system** — not
hand-drawn mockups, chip strips, or static approximations.

Reference implementation: [`brand-settings-form.tsx`](../src/components/admin/settings/brand-settings-form.tsx)
and [`brand-preview-panel.tsx`](../src/components/admin/settings/brand-preview-panel.tsx).

## Required stack

| Layer    | Component                  | Role                                        |
| -------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Layout   | `SettingsEditorShell`      | Sticky preview column + editor blocks       |
| Chrome   | `SettingsLivePreviewPanel` | Device toggle, toolbar, fullscreen, mobile  |
| Content  | `SettingsLivePreviewFrame` | Iframe + debounced `postMessage` to preview |
| Renderer | `LiveSitePreview`          | Real header, homepage sections, footer      |

## When to use

- Brand, site menu, homepage sections, media — anything owners can see on the live site
- Section-scoped previews (hero, gallery) may use `SettingsEditorShell` `sections` paired rows when the
  change is limited to one block — still prefer real components over fake markup

## Do not use for site-wide previews

- `DualDeviceSectionPreview` with custom inline mock UI (deprecated for header/menu/homepage previews)
- Bare `previews={[…]}` legacy column unless the preview is a tiny inline snippet (font size sample, color swatch)

## Adding a new settings preview

1. Load homepage sections via `loadCmsEditorData()` on the server page when the preview shows the homepage
2. Build a thin `*PreviewPanel` (e.g. `SiteMenuPreviewPanel`) that composes `SettingsLivePreviewPanel` +
   `SettingsLivePreviewFrame`
3. Pass draft overrides through `BrandPreviewPayload`:
   - Brand fields → `draft` (`BrandPreviewDraft`)
   - Nav, features, auth simulation → `site` (`SitePreviewOverrides`)
4. Wire `SettingsEditorShell` `stickyPreview={{ preview, editorBlocks }}`
5. Debounce is handled inside `SettingsLivePreviewFrame` — do not duplicate

## Site overrides (`SitePreviewOverrides`)

Use `payload.site` for non-brand draft fields:

- `nav` — menu link visibility and labels
- `features` — module toggles that affect routes or header
- `simulateAuthenticated` — show member menu links in the header preview

Merge helpers live in [`brand-settings.ts`](../src/lib/brand-settings.ts) (`applySitePreviewOverrides`).

## Copy and UX

- One sentence helper text under the preview title explaining what is live vs saved
- Device toggle (desktop / mobile) on every live preview panel
- Fullscreen expand button for homepage-style previews
- Optional audience or view toolbar (visitor vs signed-in, homepage vs sign-in) when it helps owners

See also: [`owner-friendly-ui.mdc`](owner-friendly-ui.mdc), [`responsive-design.mdc`](responsive-design.mdc).
